{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL090aGVyc19MYW5ndWFnZS9DaGluZXNlLU1vdmllcy9Gb3VyJTIwTW9vZHMlMjAlMjgxOTcwJTI5Lw","type":"movie","name":"Four Moods","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/zcjDRgdJYsR4CB761yUZK84DQOQ.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/exVx2DoXaYH48qNaYhx5IL0uYMD.jpg","description":"Directed by some of most well known Chinese-language directors of the time, the portmanteau film Four Moods was an attempt to alleviate Li Han-hsiang’s financial troubles during the late 1960s. Arguably one of his best works, King Hu’s short Anger is an adaptation of the famous Peking opera San Cha Kou; set to opera instrumentation and stylishly shot, the film deftly captures the tense showdown between political schemers, avengers and vagabonds inside an inn. Li Han-hsiang’s Happiness, inspired by the Strange Tales of Liaozhai, tells a tale of reprieve for a kind-hearted ghost, while Pai Ching-Jui’s Joy and Lee Hsing’s Sadness both explore the fateful encounters between mortal men and ghostly women.\n\nReleased 8 Oct 1970 · Taiwan · Language: Chinese · 140 min\nStudio: New Grand Films\n\nOn your server — Audio: Chinese","releaseInfo":"1970","genres":["Drama","Fantasy","Romance","Others"],"imdbRating":"6.8","imdb_id":"tt0065862","moviedb_id":287584,"tmdbId":287584,"runtime":"140 min","cast":["Zhen Zhen","Yueh Yang","Chang Mei-Yao","Li Li-Hua","Peter Yang Kwan","Chang Tseng","Han Su","Lung Fei"],"director":["Lee Hsing","Pai Ching-jui"],"writer":["Chu Hsiang-Kan","King Hu","Pu Songling"],"released":"1970-10-08T00:00:00.000Z","country":"Taiwan","language":"Chinese","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Lee Hsing","character":"Director","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/vnUlTERdGLEM44S2CA3ZQLhGuZ2.jpg"},{"name":"Zhen Zhen","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/1aBzrxbKcdROnVSiFJ2FzUAHjIE.jpg"},{"name":"Yueh Yang","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/5iqeFZAju8KNLkWidVaqRLu2eDY.jpg"},{"name":"Chang Mei-Yao","photo":"https